From 6a877fba1f4dfc697c1e8c29d3076b483f55de71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qu Wenruo <wqu@suse.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 20:43:55 +0930
Subject: [PATCH] btrfs-progs: fix the incorrectly set compression

[BUG]
The following script will lead to an incorrectly created file extent:

 # mkdir rootdir
 # xfs_io -f -c "pwrite -i /dev/urandom 0 32k" rootdir/foobar
 # mkfs.btrfs -f -r rootdir --compress zstd test.img
 # btrfs ins dump-tree -t 5 test.img
 [...]
 	item 6 key (257 EXTENT_DATA 0) itemoff 15810 itemsize 53
		generation 6 type 1 (regular)
		extent data disk byte 13631488 nr 32768
		extent data offset 0 nr 32768 ram 32768
		extent compression 3 (zstd)

Note that file extent has the same num_bytes/ram_bytes as
disk_num_bytes.

Normally this means an uncompressed extent, but it still has the
compression value set to zstd.

This will make zstd decomprssion to fail, and end users will be unable
to read that file.

[CAUSE]
Inside add_file_item_extent(), if the compression failed with -E2BIG, we
set the INODE_NOCOMPRESS flag, and fallback to the uncompressed path.

But in the uncompressed path, we still check if @do_comp is set.
And if it's set, we set the file extent compression value meanwhile the
fallback path should not go through compression at all.

The file extent compression set is a left-over from the old fallback
behavior, before the proper try_compressed_write() refactor.

[FIX]
Remove the @do_comp check and compression value set completely.

Fixes: c9c8d64acd17 ("btrfs-progs: mkfs/rootdir: factor out compressed write path from add_file_item_extent()")
Issue: #1135
Signed-off-by: Qu Wenruo <wqu@suse.com>
---
 mkfs/rootdir.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mkfs/rootdir.c b/mkfs/rootdir.c
index e2303ba119..c4932b59be 100644
--- a/mkfs/rootdir.c
+++ b/mkfs/rootdir.c
@@ -1164,9 +1164,6 @@ static int add_file_item_extent(struct btrfs_trans_handle *trans,
 	btrfs_set_stack_file_extent_num_bytes(&stack_fi, round_up(to_read, sectorsize));
 	btrfs_set_stack_file_extent_ram_bytes(&stack_fi, round_up(to_read, sectorsize));
 
-	if (do_comp)
-		btrfs_set_stack_file_extent_compression(&stack_fi, g_compression);
-
 	ret = insert_reserved_file_extent(trans, root, objectid, btrfs_inode,
 					  file_pos, &stack_fi);
 	if (ret)
